<title>AUSTRALIA: Email shares up after 5-week strike ends.</title>
<headline>Email shares up after 5-week strike ends.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in manufacturing group Email Ltd rose over four percent in early Wednesday trade after Tuesday's decision by workers at its Martin Bright steel plant to return to work after a five-week strike.</p>
<p>At 10.20 a.m. (0020 GMT), Email shares were 17 cents or 4.38 percent up at A$4.05 with about 360,000 shares traded. The shares were trading at about A$4.30 before the strike began in mid-April.  </p>
<p>Brokers said Email has also been pushed along by the positive sentiment in the share market this morning.</p>
<p>&quot;I can't see any other reasons for the rise,&quot; said one broker, in reference to the end of the strike and broader rise in the local bourse.</p>
<p>-- Kevin Morrison 61-2 9373-1813</p>
